  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;moves with a uniform speed along the circumference of a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and covers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The perpendicular projection <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> on the diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></math> represents the simple harmonic motion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. The restoration force per unit mass when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> touches <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> will be :</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/afb054e4-9d68-429e-96e6-bd5245736318-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 148px;\" /></p>",
